				<div class="cmp-teaser__content">
					<h2 class="cmp-teaser__title">
						
						Decision opens doors to DRS services for clients previously on waiting list
					</h2>
					
					
    <div class="cmp-teaser__description">
        <div class="text">
            <div class="cmp-text">
                <p><b>OKLAHOMA CITY</b> – Oklahomans with disabilities who had been on a waiting list to receive services will soon be contacted by Oklahoma Department of Rehabilitation Services staff to start their journey to joining the state’s workforce.   </p>
<p>Each month, DRS’ Performance Review Committee looks over consumer services activity reports and determines if agency and vendor resources are adequate to service additional clients who are on the Priority Group 3 waiting list. In May, committee members agreed clients could be served who were on the waiting list as of the day of the decision.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

					
    <div class="cmp-teaser__action-container">
        
    <a class="cmp-teaser__action-link" href="/okdrs/newsroom/2025/05/waiting_list_cleared.html" target="_parent" id="teaser-3546c90687-cta-d9c3c324b2" data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;teaser-3546c90687-cta-d9c3c324b2&#34;:{&#34;xdm:linkURL&#34;:&#34;/content/sok-wcm/en/okdrs/newsroom/2025/05/waiting_list_cleared.html&#34;,&#34;dc:title&#34;:&#34;Read more about waiting list changes&#34;,&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;nt:unstructured&#34;}}" data-cmp-clickable>Read more about waiting list changes</a>

    </div>

				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	
	
	
</div>

    

