					<meta itemprop="caption" content="Hellen Keller and Anne Sullivan"/>
				</div>
				<div class="cmp-teaser__content">
					<h2 class="cmp-teaser__title">
						
						DeafBlind Awareness Day
					</h2>
					
					
    <div class="cmp-teaser__description">
        <div class="text">
            <div class="cmp-text">
                <p><b>OKLAHOMA CITY</b> – Oklahoma Services for the Blind and Visually Impaired and friends will celebrate DeafBlind Awareness week June 22 – June 28 in honor of Oklahomans who are DeafBlind and world-famous author, educator, lecturer and disability advocate Helen Keller.</p>
<p>DRS’ SBVI staff will hold the 2025 DeafBlind Awareness Day from 1 p.m. to 4 p.m. on June 30 at Metro Tech, 1900 Springlake Drive in Oklahoma City. The event’s program will include the reading of a proclamation from Gov. Kevin Stitt honoring DeafBlind Awareness Week.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

					
    <div class="cmp-teaser__action-container">
        
    <a class="cmp-teaser__action-link" href="/okdrs/newsroom/2025/06/deafblind2025.html" target="_parent" id="teaser-6534523dee-cta-c71c20d40c" data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;teaser-6534523dee-cta-c71c20d40c&#34;:{&#34;xdm:linkURL&#34;:&#34;/content/sok-wcm/en/okdrs/newsroom/2025/06/deafblind2025.html&#34;,&#34;dc:title&#34;:&#34;Read more about DeafBlind Awareness Day&#34;,&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;nt:unstructured&#34;}}" data-cmp-clickable>Read more about DeafBlind Awareness Day</a>

    </div>

