               <meta itemprop="caption" content="Three young girls with Cane Quest tee shirts and metals around their necks, smile big for the camera. "/>
            </div>
            <div class="cmp-teaser__content">
               <h2 class="cmp-teaser__title">
                  
                  12th Annual Oklahoma Regional Cane Quest to  be held Nov. 6
               </h2>
               
               
    <div class="cmp-teaser__description">
        <div class="text">
            <div class="cmp-text">
                <p><b>MUSKOGEE -- </b>Oklahoma School for the Blind will be hosting its 12<sup>th</sup> annual Oklahoma Region Cane Quest with 43 eager students who are blind or visually impaired ready to prove their white cane proficiency. This competition will begin at noon on Nov. 6 at the school.</p>
<p>Contestants, with white canes as their guides, will identify obstacles and changes in surfaces, such as drop-offs at stairs or curbs, in a quest for medals and prizes. </p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

               
    <div class="cmp-teaser__action-container">
        
    <a class="cmp-teaser__action-link" href="/okdrs/newsroom/2024/11/2024-cane-quest.html" target="_parent" id="teaser-36bf7c44bb-cta-ff606bb9a8" data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;teaser-36bf7c44bb-cta-ff606bb9a8&#34;:{&#34;xdm:linkURL&#34;:&#34;/content/sok-wcm/en/okdrs/newsroom/2024/11/2024-cane-quest.html&#34;,&#34;dc:title&#34;:&#34;Read more about OSB Cane Quest Nov. 6&#34;,&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;nt:unstructured&#34;}}" data-cmp-clickable>Read more about OSB Cane Quest Nov. 6</a>

    </div>

            </div>
         </div>
      </div>
   
   
   
   
   
</div>

    
</div>
