            <div class="cmp-teaser__content">
               <h2 class="cmp-teaser__title">
                  
                  White Cane Safety  Awareness Day 2024
               </h2>
               
               
    <div class="cmp-teaser__description">
        <div class="text">
            <div class="cmp-text">
                <p>TULSA – White cane users with visual disabilities and sighted supporters will celebrate National White Cane Safety ­­­Awareness Day from 10:30 a.m. to 12 p.m. on Oct. 15 with a walk through the heart of downtown Tulsa.</p>
<p>Services for the Blind and Visually Impaired, a division of the Oklahoma Department of Rehabilitation Services, will host this year’s event. SBVI staff invites participants to gather in Williams Green Park, 61 E 3rd St, in downtown Tulsa.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

               
